map:history.summary:
The repo has 382 commits. Local master is b901339. The public remote spike/master is 50ae8e1, so master is 8 commits ahead (measured: git rev-list spike/master..master). Every change follows plan -> code -> result, with locked kill tests, mutants and byte-identity gates. The `result:` commit subjects carry the verdicts.

The work came in these phases:
1. REVIEW.md items H1-H8, M1-M17, L1-L19 and N3-N19 are all fixed. N1 moved to the transplant plan.
2. The Codex clinical review found CR1-CR9, and all reproduced. The bounded ones are fixed. CR2 and CR4 became measure-and-warn censuses. CR3 fails closed for --gvcf only. CR6 was relabelled, and af=het is now exactly 0.5.
3. T1-T7 added advisory validate rows. RF1-RF15 followed: RF6, RF13 and RF14 were fixed by del_planted and ins_planted, RF8 refuses events above SIM_RESIST 0.5, and RF12 added Recall_outside_bg.
4. --edit-model origin is experimental. It passes only the synthetic-twin physics test. Threads step 1 also landed here.
5. The HG001<->HG002 transplant ran rounds 1b, 2b and 3. Round 3 gave 5 of 16 supported, 0 refuted, 11 inconclusive.
6. Work on the hospital FASTQ route added:
   - read-length trimming and Illumina-shaped read names;
   - fastq.sh with --into-fastq;
   - the duplicate-leak fix;
   - review-20261004 fixes 1-5, 7 and 8, plus SIM_ALT_FRAGS;
   - align.sh copying the input's @PG bwa options.
7. Quality model: v1 was refuted because one event's pool was too thin. v2 learns an fqzcomp-context generator, an error table and a one-letter-run context from 20 index-placed blocks. It is merged locally but not pushed. Its speed fix sits on the unmerged quality-speed branch, which finished with exit 0 and is not yet verified.

The owner's goal is to spike clinically relevant variants (for example LDLR) into GIAB or demo data at the hospital, export a full FASTQ and run nf-core/raredisease. The owner's rules:
- model what really happens, and judge realism against real variants;
- measure before changing anything;
- merge or push only on an explicit word.

The largest open gaps:
- SNVs, indels and duplications are untested at the hospital;
- RF15: spike's short insertions are cleaner than real ones;
- spike makes no duplicates of its own reads;
- per-mate cycle counts (independent review finding 6);
- the model work in CR2, CR3, CR4, CR6, CR7 and CR9;
- origin is unvalidated on real data;
- slices were refuted as a shortcut for testing Manta and CNVnator.

limitations.what:
Architecture debt named by the independent review, all unaddressed:
- no EventPlan/EventResult; parallel index-aligned vectors carry per-event results;
- ReadPair drops read groups and molecule identity, and a multi-sample input is pooled under the first SM;
- BAM scan layers are duplicated, and census depends on validate;
- the reference is held about twice in memory;
- main.rs and validate.rs are very large;
- no run manifest or atomic publication, and no CI or pinned toolchain.

