map:synth.summary:
spike builds every planted pair from a template. For flank reads the template is the reference with the sample's SNP alleles (loh::SampleCopies holds SNPs only). Otherwise it is the edited haplotype. spike never copies donor reads. Each event draws fragment lengths from its pool's empirical |TLEN| CDF, limited to [read_length, 1500], or [1, 1500] for adapter-trimmed libraries. The number of fragments is coverage x VAF x starts / mean_frag. Coverage comes from one 2 kb window at the first breakpoint. Starts are uniform over the haplotype, or over breakpoint-crossing zones for additive events.

For each pair, a coin flip picks F1R2 or F2R1. Both templates are read in sequencing order. The two mates' read classes are drawn together from the sample's (R1, R2) class table. The draw is weighted by each mate's template one-letter-run bin and by the event's class mix. Each base then gets a quality from an fqzcomp-style context with 6 backoff levels. The context holds the recent qualities, the cycles-left bin, a change flag, the class, the lows among the last 16, and a sticky run bin. Next comes an error draw from a 4-level table: quality, class, lows, end bin, run, and errors among the last 30 bases. Both tables are learned once at startup, from 20 index-placed 50 kb blocks compared against the reference. An error is a uniform substitution, or an indel only when --indel-error-rate is above 0 (default 0). A template N gives N at Q2. Trimmed libraries cut reads to the fragment and strip 3' adapter-prefix ends.

v2 matches the sample on read-to-read spread, perfect reads and bad-end clips on 35x (K2b: 1.23-1.27% against 1.26%). Its crashed share is about 15% short. New measurements this session find gaps where the model discards structure the data has:
- the substitution spectrum (real: one dominant wrong base; spike: uniform);
- Q2 bases that are not N;
- the drop at the final cycle;
- the cycle axis of trimmed short reads;
- the fragment-end motif of the hospital library.

Known gaps also remain: homopolymer slips, duplicates, adapter read-through, and the sample's own indels (CR3). GC bias in the hospital library is small (0.88-1.08).

ideas.falsifying_measurement:
Run on the K2b design: learn the map from the even-hash pool reads, generate the odd-hash pairs at their own positions, align with bwa-mem2, and score with recur.py, inside the Q100 bench BED with Q100 masked.
- Sites with 3 or more same-strand same-alt reads must reach 0.7-1.3x real (181 -> 127-235).
- Candidates (2 or more alt reads, AF>=0.12) must reach 0.7-1.3x real (453).
- At least 40% of spike's sites with 3 or more reads must coincide (same position, strand and alt) with a real site that has 2 or more.
- Each of these must fail for broken versions:
  - master: 2 sites, 74-85 candidates;
  - the map applied at shuffled positions: overlap near the 0.0002 base rate;
  - the map with no subtraction or shrinkage: candidates above 1.3x;
  - strands swapped: overlap near 0.
If even a perfect copy of the pool's counts cannot beat 20% overlap with held-out real reads at pool depth, the idea is dead.

ideas.proposal:
In block_errors:
- key the cells by mate as well (R1/R2);
- for each counted base, also store the called base, including N, in an emission table P(called in {A,C,G,T,N} | true base, quality symbol, mate), backed off to (true, mate) and then to uniform;
- stop excluding N calls from counting.

In generate_from_template:
- after an error fires, draw the called base from the emission table instead of random_different_base;
- when the drawn quality symbol is one that the sample emits as N 99% or more of the time, emit N and skip the error draw (Q2 -> N).

Widen the learning-time variant mask to cover +-5 bp around positions where the pool reads show the sample's indels (I/D in the CIGAR, or a shared clip boundary), so the sample's indel neighbourhoods stop teaching high-Q errors.

