Each part writes JSON. A comparator checks every metric against a locked baseline JSON, with tolerances taken from the 2-seed spread. Gate merges only on a supported -> refuted flip or a discriminator or background regression beyond tolerance. Report everything else. The first use re-baselines on 4a5672d.

A locked acceptance protocol for each demo sample, with three raredisease runs at the hospital:
- the existing unspiked baseline;
- the spiked FASTQ;
- a sham FASTQ: the raw FASTQ minus a set of original pairs equal in number to the spike's removals, re-appended unchanged at the end.
Report per caller:
- sham vs baseline differences (the noise floor);
- spiked vs baseline differences outside the footprints, which must not exceed the sham;
- inside the footprints, background integrity (the first idea);
