Also audit, per event, the SPIKE_ fragments that survive into the final BAM against SIM_ALT_FRAGS, so losses in fastp, alignment or markdup become visible.

A post-processing script, kept outside the core so spike stays simple, run as: spike_truth_compose --truth truth.vcf --events events.bed --benchmark-vcf GIAB.vcf.gz --benchmark-bed GIAB.bed. It writes:
- truth.composite.vcf.gz plus .tbi: background records outside the event-copy footprints, plus the planted events, normalized with bcftools norm, with the background's sample name;
- confident.bed: the GIAB bed minus the footprints;
- strata BEDs and a hap.py stratification TSV: planted (event ±50 bp), footprint (±2 kb), and rest.
It also prints the fraction of the confident region removed, so the exclusion is never silent.

reality:M16.notes:
The reality check holds and the code change is cheap. The copy choice is a coin flipped separately for each event, even with a phased gVCF. A new seed moves the event to the other haplotype, and two LDLR exon SNVs come out cis or trans by chance. Measured on HG001 with Platinum as --gvcf: 5 cis and 1 trans over 6 seeds. Truth does not record which copy was used: GT is 0/1 and the file is identical across seeds.
Within a footprint the event already sits on one consistent real haplotype. What hap= adds is:
- control over which way round that haplotype is taken, so it can be reproduced;
- a phased GT, with PS where the gVCF has one, in the truth file;
- a logged copy choice.
I weaken rather than keep because the headline clinical impact is not real for the user's goal. The hospital raredisease run (genmod 3.9, no phased option, 0 phased GTs, no phasing step) cannot tell cis from trans for events >=7 kb apart. Inherited and de novo trio patterns are already buildable at genotype level. The phased truth sets on disk cover NA12878 only (Platinum v1.2 is limited to NA12878), and nobody has checked whether Platinum's GT order is paternal|maternal.
What remains is honest truth and reproducibility, plus a building block for M15 and M17. Cost is about S: parse the event spec, choose the block orientation in pick_target_alleles from an anchor's first_is_allele2, and change the GT writer. The work items are:
- keep the RNG draw order when hap= is absent;
- decide what to do when one block holds several PS;
- handle each side of a fusion separately;
- make reading input GT opt-in.
I wrote nothing in the repo. Scratch runs and scripts are in /tmp/claude-1066/-home-parlar-ai-dev-spike/23a35c29-9600-4da2-a2c9-618425a1e0d3/scratchpad/hapcheck/.

reality:M19.better_measurement:
Keep the mixture design: name-hash subsample of HG001 chrM at f and HG002 chrM at 1-f, from the hospital BAMs, same lane.

Change what is compared. FilterMutectCalls is not a per-site judge here, because it learns its AF clusters and its OPTIMAL_F_SCORE threshold from all calls in the sample. The mixture carries 8 sites at f and 6 at 1-f, while one spike run can hold at most 3 events, so FILTER differences would reflect the call set, not read realism.

Compare per site at the evidence level instead, before and apart from the caller:
- ALT/depth within the mixture's split-half noise;
- ALT forward/reverse ratio;
- ALT base-quality and read-position distributions;
- the share of ALT reads that are improper pairs, MAPQ<20 or duplicate-marked after re-MarkDuplicates.

Add a read-form check on ALT-carrying reads at 3107, 302 and 310. Real reads have 3107 deleted and 310 TC; synthetic reads must match. Today's binary fails this check: 5,338 synthetic reads carry C, 0 real reads do.

Then compare Mutect2 TLOD and AF per site, and FILTER only for single-site runs against single-site mixture slices.

Controls that must fail:
- diploid copy_rate (2v on the event copy);
- today's 3107 C insertion (the read-form check);
- phasing left on at HG001 16023 (0.694). Plant HG002-only 16304T>C into HG001: 16023 lies inside its ±2 kb haplotype window (281 bp away), so the coin moves 16023's level to about 0.694(1-v) or 0.694(1-v)+v (inferred). Note that 16304 is 265 bp from the chrM end, so report it with SIM_RESIST.

Drop 6210 as the FILTER yardstick, or label it as possibly recurrent.

